==========
psion/opl #1762, from dpalmer, 800 chars, Jan 19 15:3 95
Comment to 1759.
----------
REM Assuming
global item%(100)
local i%, j%, swaps%, top%, gap%, hold%, size%
size%=100

REM Combsort
gap%=size%
do
  gap%=int(gap%/1.3)

  if gap%=0
    gap%=1
  elseif (gap%=9) or (gap%=10)
    gap%=11
  endif

  swaps%=0
  top%=size%-gap%
  i%=1
  while i%<=top%
    j%=i%+gap%
    if item%(i%)>item%(j%)
      hold%=item%(i%)
      item%(i%)=item%(j%)
      item%(j%)=hold%
      swaps%=-1
    endif
    i%=i%+1
  endwh
until (gap%=1) and not swaps%
REM Sorted

I've found this to be the best sort for OPL in practice. It's 
sufficiently short to be used inline, which is essential for speed.

The problem with OPL QuickSort is that (in its recursive 
implementation) it involves lots of proc calls, which are one of the 
slowest aspects of OPL.

David.


